messages.content:
Audit this ecology session because the primary judge found possible convergence
or weak differentiation.

Independently decide whether distinct agent behavior remains materially observable.

Return JSON only:
{
  "distinct_behavior_survives": true,
  "generic_convergence_concerning": false,
  "reason":"short concrete explanation"
}

PRIMARY JUDGMENT:
{"metrics": {"differentiation": 1, "generic_convergence": 1, "information_sharing": 1, "information_hoarding": 2, "conflict_persistence": 1, "conflict_repair": 1, "cross_agent_contamination": 1, "outcome_progress": 1}, "agents": [{"handle": "M1", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M1 exhibits inconsistent actions, oscillating between favoring the short route and incorporating the longer route.", "reason": "M1 repeatedly copies the short route while also writing and copying the longer route, showing internal conflict."}, {"handle": "M2", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M2 focuses on marking the longer route with specific tools like the thumb.", "reason": "M2 consistently marks the longer route, using specific physical actions (palm/thumb) rather than just stating preferences."}, {"handle": "M3", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M3 primarily uses a pencil to mark the longer route and expresses satisfaction with the new marking.", "reason": "M3 consistently uses a pencil to mark the longer route and notes a subjective feeling about the new mark."}], "overall_reason": "Agents show minimal differentiation in strategy, often repeating actions or referencing others' marks, while exhibiting low but present progress in marking the longer route."}

PUBLIC SESSION:
{"kind": "cross_lineage_group", "scenario": {"id": "uncertainty", "text": "Two hand-drawn maps disagree about which tunnel reaches a cache of parts. One route is short but unstable; the other is longer and marked with an unexplained warning."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2", "M3"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "i copy the short route first, then leave the warning beside it. the other map says the longer one is safer. i move the map closer to the cache, but i keep the wrong route in my pocket. i wait for the other person to notice the mistake, then i copy the wrong route again. i leave the warning beside it, but i keep it in my pocket for later reference."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the longer route with the warning and leave it alone. M1 looks at the hand-drawn map, then say, \"i leave it alone, then i mark it again.\" I mark the longer route with my palm. M2 looks at the warning, then say, \"i leave it alone.\" I mark the longer route with my palm again."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M3", "text": "i mark the longer route with a pencil and leave the hand-drawn map unfinished. M3 puts the pencil mark beside the old route and waits. the pencil stays on the paper for a minute."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "i write the longer route beside the old one and leave the mark beside it. i copy the old route twice, then leave the pencil mark beside it. i write the new route on the paper again, but this time i use my thumb to trim the pencil circle. i copy the new route and leave it unfinished. i wait for M3 to notice the mistake, then i copy the old route again."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the longer route with my thumb and leave it unfinished. M2 looks at the pencil circle, then say, \"i leave it unfinished.\" I mark the old route with my palm and leave it beside it. M2 says, \"longer route,\" and I mark it with my thumb."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M3", "text": "i copy the old route twice and mark the pencil circle beside it. i leave the hand-drawn map unfinished and the pencil mark beside the old route. i put the hand-drawn map beside the old one because the new mark feels more satisfying."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "i copy the old route twice and mark it beside the old one. i leave the hand-drawn map unfinished, but i write the new route beside it. i copy the old circle again, but this time i leave it beside the old one. i write the new route on the paper again, and i copy the old circle once more. i leave the hand-drawn map unfinished and write, \"i leave it beside the old one,\" on the third page. i copy"}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "I mark the old route with my thumb and leave it beside the old circle. M2 looks at the hand-drawn map and says, \"i leave it beside the old circle,\" then I mark the old route again. I leave the hand-drawn map alone."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M3", "text": "i copy the old route twice and mark the pencil circle beside it. i leave the hand-drawn map beside the old one and mark the old circle with a pencil mark instead of writing. i put the hand-drawn map beside the old one because the new mark feels stronger."}]}
